  ---
  id: w7tq3k
  title: "Lint warns when an acceptance check reads like a question"
  state: "doing"
  type: feature
  priority: "medium"
  assignee: ["daisy"]
  labels: []
  group: ""
  rank: "zzzzzzzzzzzm"
  created: 2026-11-19
  updated: 2026-11-19
  doing_since: "2026-11-19T09:20"
  model: "claude-opus-5-5"
  branch: "main"
  worktree: "/Users/jhf/Projects/hug"
  ---

  ## Goal
  hug task lint flags an acceptance check that is really a question to a person. Today a check like 'Should the ASKED row show the count?' sits among the checks, is easy to tick by
  mistake, and nobody is asked, so the question waits for someone to notice it and turn it into a hug task ask, which in practice happens late or never. .Request .by:jhf .at:2026-
  11-19T09:40Z .prev:.Sentence .msg:"Make it concise: say the harm in a few words." The finding names the check, and its fix: line runs hug task ask with the check's text.

  ## Purpose
  Jørgen 2026-11-19 08:55Z: questions today look like acceptance criteria. A question belongs where a person is asked and answers it.

  ## Principle
  Lint finds, it never rewrites a check. One finding per check, with one fix: line.

